            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of the spleen: a rare but important differential of an acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>733.e5-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2007.11.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous rupture of the spleen, although previously documented, is a rare phenomenon. It commonly occurs in a pathologic spleen, usually owing to hematological manifestation. We describe a rare incident of spontaneous splenic rupture presenting to an emergency department as a first manifestation. The purpose of this case report is to highlight the importance of considering spontaneous rupture of the spleen as a rare but important differential of an acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
